WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.419
- Okay, newbies.
You're up.

00:00:02.419 --> 00:00:03.795
Five, six, ready, work!

00:00:03.795 --> 00:00:05.130
[dance music]

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.591
Arch those backs, kiddies!
JULES: Am I doing this wrong?

00:00:07.591 --> 00:00:10.552
I feel like Velma
searching for her glasses.

00:00:11.303 --> 00:00:13.055
- Do you know how
we're nowhere near the places

00:00:13.055 --> 00:00:14.598
we thought
we'd be in our lives?

00:00:14.598 --> 00:00:16.183
We spent the last part
of our official youth

00:00:16.183 --> 00:00:18.393
stuck inside, just here,
watering houseplants.

00:00:19.353 --> 00:00:20.854
You have too many plants!

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:22.523
JULES: I saw Wes today.

00:00:22.523 --> 00:00:24.024
- Jules?
- I didn't see you.

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:25.567
You were hiding behind
a stack of containers

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:26.944
that are made out of
clear plastic.

00:00:26.944 --> 00:00:29.738
STELLA: Are we actually seeing
Jules sexually frustrated?

00:00:29.738 --> 00:00:31.198
- I feel like
I'm in eighth grade.

00:00:31.198 --> 00:00:33.075
- Well, I can tell you
what I did in eighth grade,

00:00:33.075 --> 00:00:36.203
and it involved ruining
several electric toothbrushes.

00:00:36.203 --> 00:00:37.579
- Very graphic.

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:38.997
SINGER: It's all about me

00:00:38.997 --> 00:00:40.874
- [meow]
JULES: My life
is going nowhere.

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:41.959
[echoing] Nowhere, nowhere...

00:00:41.959 --> 00:00:43.836
- Hiya, kittens!

00:00:43.836 --> 00:00:45.212
- And here we go again.

00:00:45.212 --> 00:00:46.713
JULES: Where are they
all going?

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:49.258
- They're all taking flights
to their future,

00:00:49.258 --> 00:00:50.926
just like you two have to do.

00:00:50.926 --> 00:00:54.179
Good luck figuring out
where ya wanna go, dollface.

00:00:54.179 --> 00:00:56.139
Yee-haw!

00:00:57.182 --> 00:00:59.101
- Today is the start of
the new chapter of us.

00:00:59.101 --> 00:01:00.435
STELLA: I went to
business school

00:01:00.435 --> 00:01:01.728
to become an entrepreneur,

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.021
and we're putting up a bar
for women.

00:01:03.021 --> 00:01:05.315
A bar with rose on tap,

00:01:05.315 --> 00:01:07.109
somewhere where you can
yell at the TV

00:01:07.109 --> 00:01:08.235
while watching The Bachelor.

00:01:08.235 --> 00:01:10.112
- I just heard the words
rose and Bachelor

00:01:10.112 --> 00:01:13.365
in the same sentence, so...
yes to whatever that's for.

00:01:13.365 --> 00:01:14.825
SINGER: Let me be too much

00:01:14.825 --> 00:01:17.327
- I have decided to work hard
and see where it takes me.

00:01:17.327 --> 00:01:19.955
- I will mentor you.
Yes, I have perfect skin

00:01:19.955 --> 00:01:21.540
and I'm wildly successful,

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:22.666
but what is my legacy?

00:01:22.666 --> 00:01:24.293
- That sounded pretty good.

00:01:24.293 --> 00:01:25.627
SINGER: It's really simple

00:01:25.627 --> 00:01:27.629
STELLA: Who was that?
He was clearly hitting on you.

00:01:27.629 --> 00:01:29.381
- I thought my days of being
attracted to straight men

00:01:29.381 --> 00:01:31.800
were behind me,
and yet, here we are.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.427
SINGER: Can't they see me

00:01:33.427 --> 00:01:35.012
- You texted a guy
without my input?

00:01:35.012 --> 00:01:36.930
[echoing] Input...input?

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.932
- So what do we think
of Jules' opening here?

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.434
How did that make you all feel?

00:01:40.434 --> 00:01:41.852
- Bad.
- Ooh, he might not

00:01:41.852 --> 00:01:43.020
remember my name, let me just--

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:44.188
- No, no, no, no, no!

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:48.692
- Who thinks sending a gif
just now was a weird move?

00:01:48.692 --> 00:01:51.445
SINGER: It's really simple

00:01:51.445 --> 00:01:52.529
- I need a drink.
Pop that shit.

00:01:52.529 --> 00:01:54.198
[all squealing]

00:01:54.198 --> 00:01:56.325
JULES:
That's how friends work.

00:01:56.325 --> 00:01:58.035
Even if it's hard,
you trust each other

00:01:58.035 --> 00:01:59.494
and you show up.

00:01:59.494 --> 00:02:01.330
Remind me again why you
needed us for this?

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:04.166
- If I had one, what kind
do you think I'd have?

00:02:04.166 --> 00:02:05.792
- Circumcised?

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.753
- Is it like shoes?
Do you need to walk around

00:02:07.753 --> 00:02:09.254
the store a little,
make sure it's comfortable?

00:02:09.254 --> 00:02:11.089
- Curve or no curve?

00:02:11.089 --> 00:02:12.591
- These are the questions.

00:02:12.591 --> 00:02:14.927
SINGER: It's really simple

00:02:14.927 --> 00:02:16.637
I'm feeling good

